\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Examples of the TT-SNR-Map (top) obtained by piling up the $\rho (t)$ after the normalization procedure along with its spectrogram representation (bottom). The left panel shows Gaussian noise only, the centre panel an injected signal, and the right panel a signal with a superimposed glitch. The injected signal consists of a BNS system of $1.4 - 1.4M_\odot $ at $50$Mpc ($\rho _\mathrm  {opt} = 65.1$), while the glitch is a sine-Gaussian signal generated with parameters $f_0 = 82.74$, $Q = 232.11$, Amplitude $ A = 8.82\times 10^{-22}$, $\phi _0 = 4.01$ injected at $8.08$s before the chirp time of the BNS signal.\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
